{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789764723,"nonce":"2rlEiPjZyvdORytei8zyhG2cRcM=","title":"Interpreter aborts when a runtime helper raises: dynamic set on a missing field","message":"`var d:Dynamic = new Foo(); d.nope = 1;` under --mode interp or hybrid printed\n`hlp_throw called without active trap; aborting` and died with SIGABRT, where\n--mode jit catches \"Foo does not have field nope\". The interpreter calls\nhlp_dyn_set* straight from OSetField/ODynSet with no trap armed, so the\nruntime's hlp_error longjmps into nothing. Natives already go through\nrun_with_hl_trap; the helper calls did not.\n\nAlso the message read \"F  not have field n\": the type and field names are\nUTF-16 and were read as C strings, and the format string had lost \"does\".\n\nReproducer: scratch ThrowNative.hx (leaf sets a missing field on a class\ninstance inside a try/catch in main); run with arg 1 in each mode. Fixed by\nwrapping the three dyn-set sites in the same trap boundary a native gets\n(dyn_set_field_checked) and decoding the names as UTF-16.","files":null}]}